Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: JOIN returns too many rows

Check for missing JOIN conditions
Verify foreign key relationships
Use DISTINCT if duplicates are expected
Issue: Subquery returns multiple rows error

Use IN instead of = for multi-row subqueries
Add LIMIT 1 if only one value is needed
Verify subquery logic returns expected row count
Issue: Window function syntax error

Ensure OVER clause is present
Check PARTITION BY and ORDER BY placement
Verify column references in window frame
Issue: GROUP BY error

Include all non-aggregated columns in GROUP BY
Check for typos in column names
Verify aggregate functions are used correctly
